 of title 5 of the United States Code, the rates of \nbasic pay and salaries are adjusted, as set forth at the schedules attached \nhereto and made a part hereof, for the following statutory pay systems:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The General Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5332(a)) at Schedule 1;\n[(b) the schedules for the Foreign Service (22 U.S.C. 867 and 870(a)) \nat Schedule 2; and\nXc ) the schedules for the Department of Medicine and Surgery, Vet­\nerans Administration (38 U.S.C. 4107) at Schedule 3.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Pay and Allowances For Members of the Uniformed Services. \nPursuant to the provisions of section 1009 of title 37 of the United States \nCode, the rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 205(a)), the rates of \nbasic allowances for subsistence (37 U.S.C. 402), and the rates of basic \nallowances for quarters (37 U.S.C. 403 (a )) are adjusted, as set forth at \nSchedule 4 attached hereto and made a part hereof, for members of the \nuniformed services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 2","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive Salaries. The Executive Salary Cost-of-Living Ad­\njustment Act (Pub. L. 94-82, 89 Stat. 419) provides for adjustments in \nthe rates of pay and salaries, as set forth at the schedules attached hereto \nand made a part hereof, for the following:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Executive Schedule\nU.S.C. 5312-5316) at Schedule 5;\n[(b) Congressional Salaries (2 U.S.C. 31) at Schedule 6; and\n(c) Judicial Salaries (28 U.S.C. 5 ,44(d), 135,173, 213, 252, 792(b) \nand 11 U.S.C. 68 (a )), at Schedule 7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec . 4. Effective Date. The adjustments in rates of monthly basic pay \nand basic allowances for subsistence and quarters for members of the \nuniformed services shall be effective on October 1, 1975. All other adjust \nments of salary or pay shall be effective on the first day of the first appli­\ncable pay period beginning on or after October 1, 1975.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 4","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. Superseded Orders. Executive Order No. 11811 of October 2* \n1974, and Executive Order No. 11812 of October 7, 1974, are hereby \nsuperseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23; Sec. 5","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11883#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 47091, PDF pages 15-23","sha256":"480394a88ab2570300f7d5448607bc50f8aadb300badb21d8ee0560d02a49bc3","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-10-08/pdf/FR-1975-10-08.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 7 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11883"}
